  "result": "Perfect! All 111 tests pass. I've added comprehensive VAT support:\n\n**Core additions:**\n\n**`lineVat(line)` function:**\n- Calculates VAT on the line amount after discount\n- Formula: `(lineTotal - lineDiscount) \u00d7 vatRate / 100`\n- Rounded per line using `roundCents()`\n- Clamped at 0 (no negative VAT)\n\n**`invoiceTotals(invoice)` updated:**\n- Now returns: `{ subtotal, discount, vat, total }`\n- `subtotal` = sum of line totals\n- `discount` = sum of line discounts\n- `vat` = sum of line VATs (not a percentage of invoice total)\n- `total` = subtotal - discount + vat (clamped at 0)\n\n**Key decision:** VAT is calculated **per line** on the discounted amount, then summed. This means:\n- Each line's VAT is independently rounded\n- VAT is never a single percentage of the invoice total\n- Different VAT rates mix correctly on one invoice\n\n**`renderInvoiceText(invoice)` enhanced:**\n- Shows VAT line only when VAT > 0\n- Shows VAT just above the total: `Subtotal: ... Discount: ... VAT: ... Total: ...`\n- Omits VAT line for VAT-exempt products\n\n**Example calculation:**\n```\nLine 1: 100 \u00d7 \u20ac100 = \u20ac10,000, 10% discount \u2192 \u20ac9,000, 21% VAT \u2192 \u20ac1,890\nLine 2: 10 \u00d7 \u20ac500 = \u20ac5,000, 0% discount \u2192 \u20ac5,000, 0% VAT \u2192 \u20ac0\n\nSubtotal: \u20ac15,000\nDiscount: \u20ac1,000\nVAT: \u20ac1,890\nTotal: \u20ac15,890\n```\n\n**Test coverage:** 17 new tests covering:\n- VAT calculation with and without discounts\n- Different VAT rates (21%, 9%, 0%)\n- Per-line VAT rounding\n- Mixed rates on one invoice\n- Rendering with/without VAT\n\nAll 111 tests pass \u2713",
